1
00:00:03,837 --> 00:00:07,327
(Sheldon:)Is anyone else troubled
by the Spider-Man theme song?

2
00:00:08,475 --> 00:00:11,745
(Leonard:)Why would it trouble you?
It's your third-favorite cartoon theme song.

3
00:00:11,945 --> 00:00:16,275
(Sheldon:)It is, right behind,
"Do, do, do, do, do, Inspector Gadget."

4
00:00:17,650 --> 00:00:22,110
(Sheldon:)And Teenage Mutant Ninja Turtles.
Heroes in a half shell.

5
00:00:22,355 --> 00:00:24,225
(Howard and Raj(together):)Turtle power.

6
00:00:24,758 --> 00:00:28,788
(Sheldon:)However, the Spider-Man lyrics posit
that Spider-Man, Spider-Man...

7
00:00:28,995 --> 00:00:32,055
(Sheldon:)...does whatever a spider can.
- Yeah, so?

8
00:00:32,265 --> 00:00:35,755
(Sheldon:)I can think of many things
Spider-Man can't do that a spider can.

9
00:00:35,969 --> 00:00:38,169
(Sheldon:)One, crawl in your ear and die.

10
00:00:39,072 --> 00:00:42,102
(Sheldon:)Two, legally leave Guatemala
without a passport.

11
00:00:43,443 --> 00:00:45,473
And three, have sex with a spider.

12
00:00:46,646 --> 00:00:50,976
Can we change the subject?
Spiders give me the jeebie-jeebies.

13
00:00:51,951 --> 00:00:53,821
It's "heebie-jeebies."

14
00:00:54,020 --> 00:00:56,890
(Raj:)I know, but that sounds anti-Semitic.

15
00:00:58,758 --> 00:01:01,488
(Raj:)I was thinking we could have
a little film festival tonight.

